    "turn_text": "Welcome back. This is our number two of the Sean Hannity radio show, Leo 2.0. For those who are just tuning in, shame on you. Sean needs you for three hours every day, but I'm filling in for Sean Hannity today, Friday, October 6th. The phone in number is 1-800-941. Sean, 1-800-941. Sean, for those who don't know me, Leo 2.0. I work at Fox News. I'm a Fox News contributor, school teacher, lawyer, glad to be here, glad to try to fill the big shoes of Sean Hannity. This hour we will have President Trump on. We're just waiting for him. But I want to talk about a major historic event that took place this week. There was a motion to vacate the speaker's chair. It was successful. Kevin McCarthy is no longer the speaker. This is created some type of division within the Republican Party. And I want to talk about it. And again, they're going to have a vote next week. uh, Steve Scalise and Jim Jordan are the two announced candidates. I'm sure there's going to be others. There is rumors of President Trump being nominated as the speaker. Let me just give you. I was a history teacher, government teacher and lawyer. You do not have to be a member of Congress to become speaker. Repeat. You do not have to be a member of Congress. Look, Everyone knows, and I said this at the top of the hour. I'm a Trump Republican. Let me say that three times. I'm a Trump Republican. I am a Trump Republican. Leo, what's a Trump Republican? Okay, I'll tell you, make America great, believes in a secure border, believes in place the America first, bringing you home jobs back to America, school choice, law and order, making allies pay their fair share. I'm not a Mitch McConnell Republican. I'm not a Mitt Romney Republican. I'm not a Liz Cheney Republican. I'm not a Chris Christie Republican. I'm not a Asa Hutchison Republican. There's a difference. There is a difference. And I read people very, very well. As a lawyer, I read people. And let me tell you something about politics. There's no loyalty in politics except accept Trump supporters. And that's why they hate him. I want to repeat that. There's no loyalty in politics, folks. You could be supporting candidate A tomorrow and you turn around and stab him in the back the next day because money and power and control motivates. I would say maybe about 45% of the Republican party and maybe 99% of the Democrats. You know why they hate Trump? Because his supporters are loyal. I'm not going anywhere. I want you to understand why they hate him. He doesn't depend on the Washington donors. He doesn't depend on conventional traditional media. I will submit to you. And again, the phone number is one eight hundred nine four one Sean. No one other than Donald Trump can call for a rally on a Saturday night eight o'clock. Let's just pick a city. Fargo, North Dakota. I guarantee you, there'll be people lined up 10, 12 hours in advance. There might be 25, 30,000 people at the school auditorium. There's people outside. Name me one other politician who can do that. That's why they hate it. Because Trump supporters are loyal. and they hate that. Who hates CBS, NBC? See, they want to control the politician. The media cannot control Donald Trump. The Republican establishment cannot control Donald Trump. The rhinos hate him. The American people love him. Oh, yes. Go ahead and impeach him twice. Go ahead and indict him four times. Go ahead and try to wipe out everything he earned legally. Go ahead. It's not going to affect his base. Look at a guy like Chris Christie. Angry, jealous, resentful. That's why he's ready for president. Everyone listening to the Sean Hannity National Radio Show knows darn well, Chris Christie can't run, will never become president. Then why is he running? Because he's jealous. Asa Hutcheson, everyone listening to this program, you are fully aware that Asa Hutcheson will never be president, not in 2024. Why is he running? didn't like Sean, he didn't like President Trump. There are other candidates on that stage. They know they cannot win, but they're controlled. I want you to understand this because, you know, I read, sleep, eat politics. Know why those people are ready? They know they're not going to win the nomination. They're being controlled by the money. The donor is base. the big contributors. They're bank rolling those campaigns. You know who's bank rolling the Trump campaign? You, the American people, people like myself, I'm not going anywhere. Nothing will stop me from voting for President Trump. Nothing. Go ahead and diet them 20 more times. Not going to change. Why is he moving up in the polls? Why are his numbers increasing? Because the American people, they get it. I'm not talking about Mitch McConnell and that Washington base. I'm not talking about the Democrats. I'm not talking about MS. They will never get it. They'll never get, they cannot understand how he could draw these massive rallies, how he can have people stand in line like he's a rock star. because the american people trust it let me give you another example they try to do it apart all i think we got the president we have a president well let me just continue the brag about a number of room in about ten seconds the reason why they're jealous of him because the american people are loyal easy only candidate that the american people will not will not leave because he has a record to run on and they like what he did. And without further ado, let me bring on the man who was the 45th president, who's going to be the 47th president and who I'm going to vote for next year. President Donald J. Trump. Hello, Mr. President.",
